-- N2 example sentences, batch 5: cannot, will not, and formal occasions.
--
-- 〜ようにも〜ない is the wish blocked by circumstance; 〜もしない and
-- 〜てばかりいる are complaints about somebody else. 〜てたまらない,
-- 〜てしかたがない and 〜ずにはいられない are three degrees of not being able
-- to help it, and they sit together so the difference in strength is visible.
-- 〜てはならない prohibits. Then に当たって, に際して and を始め, which belong
-- to speeches and notices rather than conversation.
--
-- One rewording: をはじめ in kana shreds to を|は|じ|め. 始める is published,
-- so all four sentences use を始め — the same phrase in the spelling the index
-- can see, and the one a formal notice would use anyway.
--
-- Additive, idempotent, safe on a live database.

  -- you-ni-mo
  ('sent-ex-younimo-1', 'lang-ja', '行こうにも、時間がない。', 'いこう に も、じかん が ない。', 'lvl-ja-n2', 'authored', true),
